description:
Design a clock splitter that generates two output clock signals from a single input clock. The module utilizes a 2-bit counter that increments on each rising edge of the input clock. When the counter reaches a value of two, it toggles the states of both output clocks, effectively dividing the input clock frequency by two. This results in two complementary clock signals that exhibit a phased relationship, creating a higher-level clock resource for timing applications.
module top_module(
  input clk_in,
  output reg clk_out_1,
  output reg clk_out_2
);

