Design a 64x1 dual-port RAM module that operates on an 8-bit data bus. It allows writing data into one port based on a write enable signal while simultaneously reading data from another port determined by read enable signals. The address selection for both read and write operations is derived from the input data, using the lower six bits for addressing and the upper bits to control read/write functions. This setup facilitates reading from and writing to memory locations in a synchronized manner based on the clock signal, making it useful for applications requiring quick and efficient data access.
