description:
Design a signal debouncer circuit that stabilizes noisy input signals before passing them to the output. The module samples the input signal over a specified number of clock cycles, defined by the debounce_time parameter, to ensure a consistent output state. If the sampled signals match over the debounce period, the output signal reflects this stable input; otherwise, it remains in its previous state. This is particularly useful for cleaning up signals from mechanical switches or buttons to prevent multiple transitions from being registered due to noise.
module top_module(
  input wire clk,      // Added clock input
  input wire in,
  output wire out
);

code:
module top_module(
  input wire clk,      // Added clock input
  input wire in,
  output wire out
);parameter debounce_time = 10; // debounce time in clock cycles

reg [debounce_time-1:0] delay_line;
reg stable;
reg [1:0] counter;

always @(posedge clk) begin
  delay_line <= {delay_line[debounce_time-2:0], in};

  if (delay_line == {debounce_time{in}}) begin
    counter <= counter + 1;
  end else begin
    counter <= 0;
  end

  if (counter == debounce_time-1) begin
    stable <= 1;
  end else begin
    stable <= 0;
  end
end

assign out = stable ? delay_line[debounce_time-1] : in; // Fixed indexing in output assignment

endmodule

