description:
Design a 16-bit multiplier that computes the product of two 16-bit inputs, `in0` and `in1`, producing a 32-bit output. The multiplication is implemented using a sequential approach that accumulates partial products by checking each bit of `in0` and `in1`. For each set bit in `in0`, the corresponding bits in `in1` are checked, and the appropriate shifted values are added to the total sum represented by `temp`, which is then assigned to the output `out`.
module top_module(
    input [15:0] in0,
    input [15:0] in1,
    output reg [31:0] out
);

code:
module top_module(
    input [15:0] in0,
    input [15:0] in1,
    output reg [31:0] out
);reg [31:0] temp;
integer i, j;

always @(*) begin
    temp = 0;
    for (i = 0; i < 16; i = i + 1) begin
        if (in0[i] == 1) begin
            for (j = 0; j < 16; j = j + 1) begin
                if (in1[j] == 1) begin
                    temp = temp + (1 << (i + j));
                end
            end
        end
    end
    out = temp;
end

endmodule

